rules.trigger:
Already shipped since the author wrote this: yr, yrs, tbsp, Tbsp, tbs, tsp, qt, gal, doz, μg, mcg, μL, μl, μF, μA, μV, μW, Ω, kΩ, MΩ, and the folding of the micro sign. Still to add:
- Volume: cl, cL; dl, dL; fl oz, fl. oz., fl.oz.; qts; TBSP, tbsps, tblsp, tsps; pkg, pkgs.
- Mass: ng; Gt (read 'gigatons').
- Length and time: yd, yds, nmi; nm (see the nm rule); ns; wk, wks; mo, mos.
- Pressure: hPa, kPa, MPa, GPa, Pa, mbar, atm, inHg, mmHg.
- Energy and power: mAh, Ah, Wh, MWh, GWh, TWh, mW, MW, GW, kJ, kcal (MJ and GJ only after the lexicon fixes '-joules').
- Electrical: mV, kV, mA, nF, pF.
- Force and engines: Nm, N·m, lb-ft, lb ft, kN, hp.
- Other: dB, lm, lx, mpg, MPG, kts, kn, m.p.h., ppm, ppb, PB.
Add '&' to the rule's negative lookahead.
Per-symbol guards. Skip:
- hp when the sentence has game words (heal, heals, damage, potion, boss, enemy, player, mana, XP, health);
- atm unless the sentence has pressure words (pressure, psi, bar, Pa, gas, tank, dive, depth, vacuum, boiling, atmosphere);
- kn unless it has wind or boat words (it is also the Croatian kuna);
- MW when it has radio, AM, FM, kHz, station or tune;
- ppm when it has print, printer, printing, pages or scan;
- mo after 1 when a comma, '!' or the end follows;
- MJ and GJ unless energy words are near;
- PB before '&'.

review_notes:
3. Changed expectations where a native speaker reads the number two ways, or where the British 'and' is needed (that belongs to the numbers area, so it doesn't belong in units tests):
- 240 V → 12 V (US electricians say 'two-forty');
- 220 Ω → 8 Ω ('two-twenty ohm');
- 180 mmHg → 200 ('one-eighty');
- 1,200 sq. ft. → 2,000 ('twelve hundred square feet');
- 250 g → 200 g, 250g → 50g, 150 kWh/yr → 300, 250 kcal → 300;
- -0.5 V → -5 V on a supply rail (US speakers split between 'negative point five' and 'minus zero point five');
- Mt. Everest (8,849) and 980 hPa are now voice 'us'.
Two fragments became full sentences.

7. Added positives from real text:
- spec sheets: '4,000 mAh / 25 W', '7GB/s';
- UK: '2m apart', 'Fit a 13 A fuse', '75 cl';
- espresso ratios, a car review '60 mph in 4.2 s', 'Sq Ft' listings, a European 'm2' listing;
- hyphenated '12-hr shift', '3-mo trial', '3-yr-old', '5-min walk';
- nm offshore, km/L, mg/dL, mL/min, mm/s, mbar, ppm, 1 ct diamond, 34° S, 6 mo old, 2 wks;
- regression guards for mph, ml, mcg and 45°C.
Total: 115 speech cases. Above the 40–80 target, because the author's 80 lacked several common units.
